  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1109 AM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nA Heat Advisory has been issued for Tuesday for most of our non-\nPlateau counties. Heat indices are expected to reach or exceed\n105F for a large swath of the mid state. The advisory may need to\nbe extended through Wednesday, but that is much less certain. So\nfor now, we're focused on Tuesday's excessive heat. High pressure\nwill keep any weather-producing systems away from the region for\nmost of next week. The individual model solutions continue to show\na surface boundary dropping southward toward Middle Tennessee by\nweek's end, so we are introducing at least low PoPs this weekend\nand into early next week, with the possibility of a big cold\nfrontal passage right around the time of the autumnal equinox.\nHopefully, this will be the last week for excessive heat. All\nindications are that cooler weather is on the way just in time for\nthe first day of autumn.",
